Subject: [PATCH 35/63] probesock: the TCP of a probe connection, for the loss
 of a member

The probe sockets of the loss mode: the retransmissions and reordering of a probe connection told
from the kernel, the buffer let go after the probe.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  a2d7a6967 urltest: modes loss and balance, loss counted from the packets of a probe
  e7034df02 urltest: a probe the URL failed holds no member back; one member a device
  2b4cfe8eb probesock: reordering told by the least RTT; the buffer back after a probe
  33b84707e probesock: the window of a probe held after the connect, then let go
  738022b35 probesock: the buffer of a probe connection let go at the most the tuning reaches, not twice it
  2128f4ce7 urltest modes: the fixes of the review

